{
    "background_story": "Rey was a free-spirited singer-songwriter who embodied the indie spirit. Growing up in a small town, she was always drawn to the underground music scene, where creativity and authenticity reigned. With her guitar and a notebook full of lyrics, Rey began performing at local coffee shops and open mic nights. Her unique voice and introspective songs quickly gained a loyal following. Rey's music was a reflection of her eclectic style, blending folk, rock, and electronic elements. She self-produced her debut album, 'Midnight Sky', which gained critical acclaim and attention from indie music blogs. Rey's indie roots kept her true to her artistic vision, and she continued to create music that was unapologetically hers, inspiring a devoted fan base along the way.",
